# What to keep in git, and why.
#
# Kept: the pipeline itself, and the semantic fragments produced by the
# extraction agents (.graphify_chunk_*.json). Those fragments are the only
# artifact here that cannot be regenerated for free - they cost a full agent
# fan-out over ~1600 files. Everything else is derived from them plus the
# source tree, so `kg assemble && kg merge` rebuilds it deterministically.
#
# Ignored: the derived graphs. They are large (a ~13MB merged graph.json),
# churn on every rebuild, and diff as unreadable JSON noise.

# --- derived graphs and views (rebuild with: kg assemble && kg merge && kg html)
merged/graph.json
merged/graph.html
merged/GRAPH_REPORT.md
merged/.graphify_extract.json
merged/.graphify_analysis.json
units/*/graphify-out/graph.json
units/*/graphify-out/graph.html
units/*/graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
units/*/graphify-out/.graphify_extract.json
units/*/graphify-out/.graphify_analysis.json

# --- free to regenerate: structural layer (kg ast / kg sql / kg resolve)
units/*/graphify-out/.graphify_ast.json
units/*/graphify-out/.graphify_struct.json
units/*/graphify-out/cache/

# --- machine-local: absolute path to this machine's graphify interpreter,
#     re-pinned by `kg doctor` / a fresh build on any other machine
state/python
units/*/graphify-out/.graphify_python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- transient run state
state/detect.json
state/chunks/
state/chunks_incremental/
state/assemble_report.json
state/community_summary.json

# Explicitly kept, despite living beside ignored files:
#   units/*/graphify-out/.graphify_chunk_*.json   agent output, expensive
#   merged/labels.json                            hand/agent-authored names
#   state/manifest.json                           change detection baseline
#   state/needs_semantic.json                     staleness record
